{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"vegan-lowish-liger","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Document how to clone this repo cheaply, state the one accepted degradation honestly, and fix the\nlatent wrong-answer bug that degradation would otherwise cause. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Doc\nRecord `--filter=blob:none` guidance with the measured numbers (full **1.04 GiB / 59 s** vs blobless\n**68.7 MiB / 14.3 s**), and that `--filter=tree:0` must never be used here (measured **3.57 GiB**,\n3.4x larger than full). Note that rebar itself cannot filter a clone it does not perform.\n\n## The code fix (why it belongs with the doc)\n`git blame` over historical trees runs on a real rebar path: `metrics/blame.py:69` <-\n`_blame_file_commits` <- `derive_caused_by` (`:94`) <- `transition_close.py:513`, i.e. **on every bug\nclose without an explicit `--caused-by`**. Under a blobless promisor this faults blobs one at a time.\n\nTotal failure is benign (`blame.py:37` returns `None`). **Partial failure is not:**\n`derive_caused_by` loops per path and tallies across all of them, so if blame succeeds on some paths\nand fails on others — entirely plausible with a partly-warm object store — the strict-majority test\nruns over a **subset** and can elect a culprit that would not have won over the full set. That writes\na **wrong `caused_by` link**, which is worse than writing none.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `derive_caused_by` returns `None` when `_blame_file_commits` fails for **any** path, rather than\n      tallying a partial set. Tier: **unit** injecting a per-path failure.\n- [ ] No `caused_by` link event is written in that case. Tier: **integration** on the close path\n      asserting the event set.\n- [ ] With all paths succeeding, the derived culprit is unchanged from today — the negative control.\n      Tier: **unit** golden comparison.\n- [ ] The guidance doc exists, states the measured numbers, names the accepted `git blame`\n      degradation, and is linked from the docs index. Tier: **doc-existence + content check**.\n\n## Files\n`src/rebar/metrics/blame.py`, `docs/` guidance page, tests\n\nScope: S. No dependencies.","id":"42fa-676d-fbbb-4ac5","parent_id":"42eb-5789-c798-4dfc","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"B4: clone-guidance doc + make derive_caused_by abort on any per-path blame failure"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785372546159906001,"uuid":"3b155daf-4d59-422b-a22e-7a344115d600"}